examples.question_text:
Calculate the area of this L-shaped floor.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[thick,black] (0,0)--(8,0)--(8,2)--(3,2)--(3,5)--(0,5)--cycle;
\node[below] at (4,0) {$8\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (8,1) {$2\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (1.5,5) {$3\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,2.5) {$5\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Split the floor into two rectangles. The lower right rectangle has width $8-3=5\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[thick,black] (0,0)--(8,0)--(8,2)--(3,2)--(3,5)--(0,5)--cycle;
\draw[dashed,black] (3,0)--(3,2);
\node at (1.5,2.5) {$A_1$};
\node at (5.5,1) {$A_2$};
\node[below] at (5.5,0) {$5\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}A_1&=3\times5\\&=15\text{ m}^2\end{align*}$
$\begin{align*}A_2&=5\times2\\&=10\text{ m}^2\end{align*}$
$\begin{align*}A&=A_1+A_2\\&=15+10\\&=25\text{ m}^2\end{align*}$

examples.question_text:
A U-shaped floor has an overall width of $12\text{ m}$ and height of $7\text{ m}$. Each side arm is $3\text{ m}$ wide and the bottom strip is $2\text{ m}$ high. Calculate its area.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=4mm,y=4mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[thick,black] (0,0)--(12,0)--(12,7)--(9,7)--(9,2)--(3,2)--(3,7)--(0,7)--cycle;
\node[below] at (6,0) {$12\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,3.5) {$7\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (1.5,7) {$3\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (10.5,7) {$3\text{ m}$};
\draw[<->,black] (13,0)--(13,2);
\node[right] at (13,1) {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Split the floor into a bottom rectangle and two upper arms. Each upper arm has height $7-2=5\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=4mm,y=4mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[thick,black] (0,0)--(12,0)--(12,7)--(9,7)--(9,2)--(3,2)--(3,7)--(0,7)--cycle;
\draw[dashed,black] (0,2)--(3,2) (9,2)--(12,2);
\node at (6,1) {$A_1$};
\node at (1.5,4.5) {$A_2$};
\node at (10.5,4.5) {$A_2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}A_1&=12\times2\\&=24\text{ m}^2\end{align*}$
$\begin{align*}A_2&=3\times5\\&=15\text{ m}^2\end{align*}$
$\begin{align*}A&=A_1+2A_2\\&=24+2(15)\\&=54\text{ m}^2\end{align*}$

examples.question_text:
A shed wall consists of a rectangle $9\text{ m}$ wide and $4\text{ m}$ high, with a triangle of perpendicular height $2\text{ m}$ joined along its top. Calculate the area of the wall.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[thick,black] (0,0)--(9,0)--(9,4)--(4.5,6)--(0,4)--cycle;
\draw[dashed,black] (0,4)--(9,4) (4.5,4)--(4.5,6);
\draw[black] (4.5,4.3)--(4.8,4.3)--(4.8,4);
\node[below] at (4.5,0) {$9\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (9,2) {$4\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (4.5,5) {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A window consists of a rectangle $4\text{ m}$ wide and $3\text{ m}$ high, with a semicircle joined along its top. Calculate its area to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[thick,black] (0,3)--(0,0)--(4,0)--(4,3) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=2];
\draw[dashed,black] (0,3)--(4,3);
\node[below] at (2,0) {$4\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$3\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the area of this trapezium by splitting it into a rectangle and a triangle. Then check using the trapezium formula.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=4mm,y=4mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[thick,black] (0,0)--(12,0)--(7,6)--(0,6)--cycle;
\draw[black] (0,0.4)--(0.4,0.4)--(0.4,0);
\node[below] at (6,0) {$12\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (3.5,6) {$7\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,3) {$6\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The triangle's base is $12-7=5\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=4mm,y=4mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[thick,black] (0,0)--(12,0)--(7,6)--(0,6)--cycle;
\draw[dashed,black] (7,0)--(7,6);
\draw[black] (7,0.4)--(7.4,0.4)--(7.4,0);
\node at (3.5,3) {$A_1$};
\node at (8.5,2) {$A_2$};
\node[below] at (9.5,0) {$5\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$A_1=7\times6=42\text{ m}^2$
$A_2=\frac12\times5\times6=15\text{ m}^2$
$\begin{align*}A&=A_1+A_2\\&=42+15\\&=57\text{ m}^2\end{align*}$
Check using the parallel sides and perpendicular height.
$\begin{align*}A&=\frac12(12+7)\times6\\&=57\text{ m}^2\end{align*}$

examples.question_text:
A wall is $7\text{ m}$ wide and $4\text{ m}$ high. An arch cut from the wall consists of a rectangle $3\text{ m}$ wide and $2\text{ m}$ high, with a semicircle of diameter $3\text{ m}$ on top. Calculate the remaining wall area to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[thick,black] (0,0)--(0,4)--(7,4)--(7,0)--(5,0)--(5,2) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=1.5] --(2,0)--cycle;
\draw[dashed,black] (2,2)--(5,2);
\node[above] at (3.5,4) {$7\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,2) {$4\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (3.5,0) {$3\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (5,1) {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
